TheNextLevel on openSUSE
========================

This is the original 1996 configuration (not Red Hat's 1997 variant with
Windows 95 style buttons), ported to fvwm 2.7. Pick "TheNextLevel" in the
display manager's session list.

Files
-----
/etc/X11/TheNextLevel/.fvwm2rc.m4   main m4 source, run through FvwmM4
/etc/X11/TheNextLevel/.fvwm2rc.*    the files it reads
/etc/X11/TheNextLevel/.Xdefaults    X resources merged at session start
/usr/share/thenextlevel/pixmaps     icons and title bar buttons

Each .fvwm2rc.* file is read from your home directory if you have a copy
there, so to change the user options:

  cp /etc/X11/TheNextLevel/.fvwm2rc.defines ~/
  $EDITOR ~/.fvwm2rc.defines

and pick "Restart Fvwm2" from the System Utilities menu. Personal icons can
go in ~/.fvwm/icons.

The user documentation is docs/index.html in this directory ("Help Fvwm" in
the root menu).

Changes from the original
-------------------------
- Installed system wide (the per-file $HOME override is Red Hat's idea).
- fvwm 2.7 syntax: ImagePath, ButtonStyle Pixmap, Style * Font,
  new MenuStyle and EdgeResistance, TitleStyle "-- Raised".
- Fonts use a fixed pixel size, and the title bar is FONT_SIZE+6 pixels
  high (TITLE_HEIGHT) to fit the 18 pixel buttons. Text centering in a
  title bar this size needs the fvwm2 package from home:caiocco.
- The xlock menus list the original modes that the installed xlockmore
  still has (AUTO_XLOCK_OPTIONS would add ~140 modes).
- Menu entries for modules removed from fvwm (FvwmConfig, FvwmSave,
  FvwmScroll, FvwmClean) are gone; Window List uses FvwmIconMan.
- Msgs runs journalctl, Help opens with xdg-open, Root shell uses "su -".
- The zsh, emacs, xdm, console keymap and control-panel parts of the
  original Install.sh are not installed.
